+# SOCC log: newly observed production-page locators
+
+October 31, 2026. Existing telephone-source work, TEL02/TEL04 and TEL-NI-TIME. This supplements the [preceding partial log review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/565a624e10d986a83865d3c0f239db8ba75a707f/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-socc-later-leads-2026-10-30/README.md) with four exact page labels that were previously unobserved. It does not replace the source, earlier readings, uncertainty or original-record requirements.
+
+## New observations and prior state
+
+The [same public SOCC-log mirror](https://www.scribd.com/document/16762194/T7-B20-Timelines-9-11-2-of-2-Fdr-AA-SOCC-Log-Redacted-Version) displays the following footer labels. Each was read directly in its own visible page context; the values were not inferred from neighboring page numbers.
+
+| Viewer page and visible printed page count | Newly read production label | Preserved prior observation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 9 of 32 | **AA KEAN COMM 002538** | Bates label not observed/recorded in preceding review |
+| 10 of 32 | **AA KEAN COMM 002539** | Lower page/footer not inspected; Bates label not observed |
+| 11 of 32 | **AA KEAN COMM 002540** | Lower page/footer not inspected; Bates label not observed |
+| 12 of 32 | **AA KEAN COMM 002541** | Footer not inspected; Bates label not observed |
+
+These are **specific retrieval keys for an agency/production counterpart**, not authenticated proof of an agency release, complete native log, author, transmission, recipient receipt or recording survival. The earlier unobserved/null entries describe the earlier reading scope; those original notes remain unchanged. The newly visible values are added with their own provenance rather than silently rewriting that state. Sequential-looking labels do not prove that intervening original records are complete or that the page count is a complete record inventory.
+
+## Reading actually performed
+
+Eight browser screenshot views covered portions of four viewer pages: 9–12. One view was an orientation overlap with previously inspected content and one repeated the page-12 footer for preservation. Additional inspected regions were page 9's middle/lower entries and footer, page 10's lower entries/footer, page 11's lower entries/footer, and page 12's lower entries/footer. This remains a **partial review**, not a complete four-page or 32-page reading. The page-10 middle gap and other unseen regions/pages remain untested.
+
+No completed recording delivery/save/transfer confirmation was identified in the newly inspected regions. That is a bounded negative reading, not proof that no such entry or recording exists. The new material mainly concerns later operational and notice activity. Incidental display, baggage, personnel-status and airport-operation entries were not promoted into recording failures, survivor claims, attack-day timing or conspiracy evidence.
+
+The printed footer **1/15/02 7:21** remains a displayed label, not independently authenticated creation, event, recording or print time. Page 9's governing date header was not observed; do not assign its rows to September 11. The visible September 13 boundary/context on later pages does not calibrate all row clocks. Prior blanks, estimates, conflicting event labels, conditional retrieval language, PASSUR-data-holder lead, anticipated notice retraction and missing NOTAM/advisory originals remain unchanged. Those earlier entries are not newly corroborated merely because another part of the same log is now readable.
+
+## Provenance and checks
+
+This source remains a **public mirror reader**. No native PDF, original electronic log, agency release/attachment manifest or custody chain was acquired in this unit. The source PDF SHA-256 is therefore **unknown**, not borrowed from a screenshot or another document. The reader's changed URL spelling and page fragment are navigation details, not a source-version change established by this review.
+
+One code-free screenshot of the visible page-12 footer was preserved locally, excluded from the public payload. Its SHA-256, recorded in [PROVENANCE.json](PROVENANCE.json), identifies that **JPEG browser capture only**. Other raw frames containing possible contact/access-code fields were not saved as new public artifacts. No contact/code was used and no obscured content reconstructed. Raw source pages, screenshots, identifiers/contact fields, private correspondence and case strategy are excluded from this public derivative.
+
+A single exact-label query restricted to Archives.gov, GovInfo.gov and FBI.gov did not return a counterpart. That search is not a repository census or proof of nonexistence, withholding or destruction. Two separately logged federal-oversight queries also failed to locate the FAA correction/disposition counterpart; unrelated results were not promoted to case evidence or downloaded to manufacture progress. No fee, request/filing, outreach, mailbox access or login/download/paywall bypass occurred.
+
+[PROVENANCE.json](PROVENANCE.json) pins each new label to its page/footer and preserves actual capture/source distinctions. [VERIFICATION.json](VERIFICATION.json) records actual preservation/reference checks and limits; no decoding, call matching, recording continuity, clock fitting, independent analyst verification or historical authenticity test was performed. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) is the exact additive research-text diff, not a source-log version diff. The [preceding report](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/565a624e10d986a83865d3c0f239db8ba75a707f/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-socc-later-leads-2026-10-30/README.md) and [its TODOs](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/565a624e10d986a83865d3c0f239db8ba75a707f/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-socc-later-leads-2026-10-30/OBSERVATIONS-AND-TODOS.json) remain preserved, with no source-wording correction or causal adjudication.
+
+## Next discriminating records
+
+Use the exact production labels to seek the agency copy and native parent/version, full attachment and release/production manifest, and the timeline/annotations actually used in the interviews. Then join any recording-retrieval references to original tape identifiers, copying/extraction logs, transfer/receipt records, media contents and event/clock definitions. The new labels do not establish those joins.
+
+All eighteen requirements across FAA, telephone, recorder, materials and steel remain open or partial. No substantive criterion is closed by this locator supplement, the negative search or publication. [OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) retains the existing telephone IDs and their native-input dependencies; the original five-track scope and owner assignments remain intact. Publication/remote file verification is a separate step from acquisition, authentication, testing and substantive acceptance.
